# The libmtlc revision this tree builds against.
#
# libmtlc (https://github.com/The-Mettle-Project/libmtlc) is Mettle's compiler
# backend: the IR, the optimizers, code generation and native linking. Mettle
# supplies the language and the frontend; everything after IR lowering is
# libmtlc's. get-libmtlc.ps1 / get-libmtlc.sh fetch the revision named here.
#
# Any git revision works: a release tag (v0.13.0), a branch (main), or a commit
# SHA. A SHA or tag is what makes a build reproducible; `main` tracks
# development and will drift under you. Override for one build with
# LIBMTLC_VERSION, or point LIBMTLC_DIR at a local libmtlc checkout to skip the
# download entirely.
#
# Moving this pin changes the generated code, so treat it like a codegen change:
# run the differential fuzzer before trusting it (see CONTRIBUTING.md). The
# driver also calls into backend headers directly, so a pin older than a call
# site in src/main.c fails to compile rather than silently misbehaving --
# libmtlc has to have the API before this can point at it.
dfa62b734357307b68e90a05ebd005c86b07c503
